Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Covariant Derivatives and Connections in the \[ScriptCapitalU]\
\[ScriptCapitalD] Calculus", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.976889187114873*^9, 3.9768892175197353`*^9}, {
  3.977098182469513*^9, 
  3.977098186708535*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e32a3f2a-fb9c-4256-a2ab-\
ff2d5896380e"],

Cell["Brian Beckman", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.5011898003565187`*^9, 3.5011898164415183`*^9}, {
  3.970503905858189*^9, 3.970503938930399*^9}, {3.9705040303289137`*^9, 
  3.970504033015139*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"8531c00f-1b9c-4144-b1cc-\
d974e69c32ba"],

Cell["Jan 2026", "Author",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.970503954212903*^9, 3.97050395891148*^9}, {
  3.972479129640115*^9, 3.9724791301125593`*^9}, {3.973546918457328*^9, 
  3.973546918968728*^9}, {3.9762809550919313`*^9, 
  3.976280957806756*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"90e60fd9-e338-4487-becf-\
9813ab59ecef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977148675925516*^9, 
  3.977148677656872*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"578e7ca6-7fb8-431d-bd76-\
b4fe5885c110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this installment of the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] Calculus \
series, we tackle the central mechanical hurdle of general relativity: how to \
take a derivative on a curved manifold without breaking invariance against \
choice of coordinates. Standard partial differentiation fails to be \
tensorial, creating garbage terms during coordinate transformations. We solve \
this by introducing the covariant derivative and its necessary correction \
term, the connection coefficient (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CapitalGamma]", TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5da03282-23ef-43f3-8f59-e683d4197ba7"],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977327877192577*^9, 3.977327934355731*^9}, {
  3.97733134555328*^9, 3.9773313602738132`*^9}, {3.977344805844727*^9, 
  3.977344822014463*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"099efbbb-d635-442a-91e5-\
bef6097ac8bd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Using a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]glass-box\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] approach\
\[LongDash]where the RelativityToolkit is exposed for inspection rather than \
hidden behind a package\[LongDash]we computationally derive the non-tensorial \
transformation law of \[CapitalGamma]. Finally, we apply the constraints of \
Metric Compatibility (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[Del]", "g"}], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "f76e9cbd-960b-4526-8651-184ea4f5f422"],
 ") and Torsion-Free geometry to derive the famous Christoffel Symbols ",
 StyleBox["ab-initio",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". This derivation, often called the Fundamental Theorem of Riemannian \
Geometry, is performed step-by-step in the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] \
engine, demonstrating that the index gymnastics of gravitation are \
algorithmic consequences of simple geometric demands and Wolfram\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s algebraic support."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977327877192577*^9, 3.977328021128574*^9}, 
   3.977331334704853*^9},ExpressionUUID->"5d2a3e38-cf35-49d5-91d1-\
2eef83b96ca6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Audience", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153047020433*^9, 
  3.977153048226739*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bdec919a-8323-46cd-938b-\
759ef07283ee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This series of notebooks is targeted at readers with an undergraduate\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s STEM education\[LongDash]engineering, computer science, \
mathematics, with perhaps introductory courses in Classical Mechanics (e.g., ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Goldstein",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/aGDvq6V"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/aGDvq6V"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "), Electrodynamics (e.g., ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Jackson",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/1L0vvD3"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/1L0vvD3"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "), and Relativity (e.g., ",
 StyleBox[ButtonBox["Schutz",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://a.co/d/5iVgPNn"], None},
  ButtonNote->"https://a.co/d/5iVgPNn"],
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 "). "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153053944147*^9, 3.977153244196105*^9}, {
  3.977324364580159*^9, 3.977324411077203*^9}, {3.977324444683196*^9, 
  3.977324508468995*^9}, {3.977325843557014*^9, 3.977325845658771*^9}, {
  3.9773259838117332`*^9, 3.97732599552731*^9}, {3.9773260299933157`*^9, 
  3.977326044248126*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0ea1c893-ac06-4633-be91-\
6ddb165c9ed5"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["By and large, I do not put standard textbooks in the \
References section, but offer clickable (non-affiliate!) links instead in the \
prose of this notebook.",
 FontSlant->"Italic"]], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9773258649129257`*^9, 3.977325912216382*^9}, {
  3.977326673610219*^9, 3.9773266776011953`*^9}, {3.977331695334305*^9, 
  3.9773317026496477`*^9}, {3.97734264868922*^9, 
  3.977342662845957*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20adb044-20b4-426a-8192-\
436dec75131b"],

Cell["\<\
I also invite readers to \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]think like a physicist,\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] that is, to demand conceptual cogency, but not \
always full mathematical rigour.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977153053944147*^9, 3.977153244196105*^9}, {
  3.977324364580159*^9, 3.977324411077203*^9}, {3.977324444683196*^9, 
  3.977324497152054*^9}, {3.977342669832375*^9, 
  3.9773426825067263`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"933e3ac1-018e-4b73-b45a-\
f9259451c097"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Transparent Implementation", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, 3.976889556697713*^9, 3.976889851295733*^9, {
   3.977097211709004*^9, 3.977097213201786*^9}, {3.977148398602599*^9, 
   3.977148408725576*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5c85bee8-6fff-4c6e-ba13-\
21ee29fd942b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In developing the \[ScriptCapitalU]\[ScriptCapitalD] Calculus, we made a \
conscious decision for the time being to implement the engine as a glass-box ",
 StyleBox["script",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " rather than as a Package, prioritizing transparency over isolation at this \
stage of development. When the toolkit is finalized in the future, we\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll address encapsulating it in a Package."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.9768895935975227`*^9}, {
   3.9769715522630987`*^9, 3.976971581002223*^9}, 3.9770969722863827`*^9, {
   3.9770970369338617`*^9, 3.977097104142345*^9}, 3.977099003004167*^9, {
   3.9770990471939573`*^9, 3.977099055974069*^9}, {3.97714842661103*^9, 
   3.977148428181637*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ad9d1db-a459-453c-8a0f-\
ab0ff2d3dcce"],

Cell["With this glass box, the reader can:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.9768896868815203`*^9}, {
   3.977097109877501*^9, 3.97709711259033*^9}, {3.977148434120612*^9, 
   3.977148436413513*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"33d29148-4fb9-4c6d-b1a1-\
1cb356be3429"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Inspect the machinery: Type ",
 StyleBox["?valence", "Input"],
 " or ",
 StyleBox["?metricRules", "Input"],
 " and immediately see the physics logic, not an opaque symbol."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 
   3.976889704406357*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"65f78dce-8047-4c0d-b6fa-\
568aac671db2"],

Cell["\<\
Modify the engine: Experiment with new rules without fighting a locked \
namespace.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.97688929871796*^9, {3.976889563666814*^9, 3.97688971686047*^9}, {
